+        "LayoutEditor__SelectionBindings__Description": "What a modifier held on a Select tool press does to the selection - for a click on an item and for a box dragged from bare paper alike - as SketchUp holds them. With none held the click or the box replaces the selection. The list is tested in order with Exact matching, so the two-modifier binding sits first. BoxAnywhereModifier is set aside before the list is tested: while it is held a drag draws a box even from on top of something that could be moved, which is the way in on a sheet with no bare paper left to start from, and Shift or Ctrl still combine with it. A box dragged to the right is a window (only what it wholly encloses); dragged to the left it is a crossing (anything it touches as well). CopyDragModifier is SketchUp LayOut's copy by drag: held on the press of a move, or pressed during one, the move carries a copy and leaves the original where it was, and pressed again it is a move again - a tap is enough, so it can be let go of to reach the arrow keys or type a length. It is not set aside like BoxAnywhereModifier: Ctrl still adds an unselected item at the press, and the drag then copies the whole selection. A viewport or a dimension copies only where it would move, under the Move tool. Leave it empty to switch copying by drag off. MoveAnchorModifier puts the move anchor on an item: held ON ITS OWN through a click that leaves one item or one group selected, a red cross comes up in the middle of its box, with the Move tool. Drag the cross onto any snap point to re-place it (double-click it to centre it again); drag the item and it is carried by the cross alone, which snaps - so it moves from this point to that point. It is not set aside either: Ctrl still adds on the press and copies on a drag, so with something else already selected a Ctrl+click adds and no cross comes up. Leave it empty to switch the cross off; its look and settings are in 28__System__ObjectSnap/Na__LayoutEditor__MoveAnchor__Config__.json.",
