+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__HeightMmNote": "LANTERN DESIGNER'S STRIP: 10 mm, the height the two apps share, so a drawing from either sits in one pack. THE QR CODE IS AS TALL AS THIS ALLOWS - the strip's height less the symbol's quiet zone - so this is also what decides whether a phone can read a printed drawing: 10 mm prints the project's 29 module symbol at 0.303 mm a module in an 8.79 mm square, which is Lantern Designer's own 8.8 mm code with a larger module than Lantern's 0.267. DO NOT LOWER IT: the console says so whenever the module falls under the floor set in Na__ProjectQr__Config__.json. History: 16 mm once, with each value pinned to the foot of the strip, which read as an empty box with writing in its corners; 10 to match Lantern Designer; 20 for one day (19-Sep-2026) while the code carried the project's full 135 byte address and needed the height, which Adam judged 'too tall, too portrait-feeling, and stretched'; and 10 again on 20-Sep-2026, when the code was given a 42 byte address instead (ProjectQr__Link__LengthNote in that file). Raising it is safe for the code, which simply grows with it - but placed viewports are never moved, so a taller strip can run over drawings already laid out against this one.",
