+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__RowsNote": "WidthMm IS PAPER MILLIMETRES, the same on every paper size, the way the logo already is. Until 20-Sep-2026 these were relative shares of the strip, so every cell grew and shrank with the paper: on A2 the Client cell was 76 mm for a surname and the Drawing No. 49 mm for eight characters, while on A3 the Drawing Title - the one value that is ever long - had 71 mm and cut an 88 mm title short. Authored in TrueVision3D v2.79.0 to Adam's brief there: 'there are certain fields that are never going to need more size, so they kind of seem needlessly oversized... The one thing that does need the space is the drawing name.' A row with Flex takes what the paper has left over, shared by weight if more than one has it, and its WidthMm is the least it is ever given; the Drawing Title is the one that ships with it. NO VALUE IS CUT OFF WHILE ANOTHER CELL HAS ROOM TO SPARE: a cell whose text will not fit grows, out of the paper's spare room first and then out of the room other cells are not using, which is how Site Address and the title 'grow if absolutely required'. A pack whose values fit therefore has its dividers in the same place on every sheet. On paper too narrow for the strip (A4) the cells give up their unused room before anything is cut. The arithmetic is Na__LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__Cells__.js. THE WIDTHS ARE TRUEVISION'S, so the two apps issue the same strip, and were re-measured here in this app's own face - jsPDF's Helvetica at FontSizeValueMm, padding included - because Helvetica sets wider than TrueVision's Open Sans: Client 36 holds 'Mr & Mrs Featherstonehaugh' (31.2); Site Address 70 holds '255 Musters Road, West Bridgford, Nottinghamshire, NG2 7DD' (64.2); Drawing No. 24 holds a typed 'PS01_T02_D100' (19.5) and the 3047-01 default with room over; Rev, Scale, Date and Drawn By are one 28 mm module, set by the widest thing any of them says - '1:50 & 1:100 @ ISO A2' (25.7), with Drawn By's default 'Vale Garden Houses' 