+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__ValuePrefixNote": "A row's ValuePrefix is printed in front of its value, with a space, whenever there is a value to print. It is how the Rev cell reads 'Revision A' rather than a lone letter - Adam, 21-Sep-2026: 'it looks a bit silly with just a letter in'. It is PRINTED, never stored: the sheet still holds 'A', so the Drawing Register's column, the Sheet panel's box and the PDF file name's {revision} token (RevA) are all unchanged. A value that already starts with the prefix or a word it begins with ('Rev B', 'Revision B') keeps only the letter, so it can never print 'Revision Rev B'. An empty value prints nothing, prefix included. A prefix never costs another cell its text: on a strip too narrow for every value whole (A4 portrait) the builder solves it again with the bare values, and the cell prints 'A'.",
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__RowWidthFactorByPaperNote": "Every row EXCEPT the Flex ones (the Drawing Title) is this much wider on the paper named - Adam, 21-Sep-2026: on A2 and A1 give the site address and each box on the right '20% more space', the drawing title excepted. Paper sizes not listed use the rows as they are. THE FIFTH IS ON WHAT THE CELL PRINTS AT, not on its WidthMm: RB05's site address had already grown its 70 mm cell to 84 to fit, and a fifth on the 70 would have been 84 again - no air at all for the one cell Adam pointed at; it is 100.8 now. THE EXTRA IS PAID ONLY OUT OF THE DRAWING TITLE'S SPARE ROOM, never out of its text: the cells take their fifth only while the strip still has room once every cell - the title included - has the wider of its WidthMm and its text; where it cannot afford all of it (A2 portrait, whose strip is A3 landscape's) every cell gets the same smaller share, down to none. On A2 landscape the fields are left 488 mm between the logo and the QR cell: 272 mm of fixed rows become 326.4, and the title keeps 161.6 of its 216. The logo cell and the QR cell are not rows and do not grow - the QR cell's width is measured to set its note in two even lines. The arithmetic is Na__LeTitleCells__Widen.",
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__RowWidthFactorByPaper": { "A2": 1.2, "A1": 1.2 },
