+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellNote": "THE RIGHT-HAND END OF THE STRIP IS THE PROJECT'S QR CODE AND A NOTE SAYING WHAT SCANNING IT DOES, so anybody holding a drawing can point a phone at it and be standing in the 3D model. It mirrors the logo cell at the left: an absolute width in paper millimetres off the end of the strip, the same on every paper, with the Rows solved across what is left between the two - so Status is the last FIELD and this cell stands beyond it, in the sheet's bottom right corner. It is modelled on Lantern Designer's terms cell, and at this strip height it is that cell's size: an 8.79 mm code with 0.61 mm round it. These keys say WHERE the code goes and how its note is set. WHAT it says - the address, the words, the symbol's colours, quiet zone and smallest readable module - belongs to the Project QR Code system: 02__Src__AppModules/53__Feature__ProjectQrCode/Na__ProjectQr__Config__.json. The code needs no size here: it is the strip's HeightMm less the quiet zone it is owed, so it follows the strip. With no project on the address bar, or with that system switched off, there is no cell and the fields keep the whole strip.",
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellEnabled": false,
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellWidthMm": 56,
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellWidthMmNote": "The whole cell: the note's column, then the code with its clear margin either side. The code and its margins take 10 mm of this, PaddingHMm and TextGapMm another 2.4, which leaves the note a column of 43.6 mm. MEASURED, NOT GUESSED: every width from 42 to 58 was wrapped against the shipped words in Open Sans at three body sizes, and this column is the one that sets the body at 1.5 mm in TWO LINES OF ALMOST EXACTLY EQUAL LENGTH - '...and view the building' over 'in full 3D, and to freely navigate and take a tour.' - flush without any letter spacing to speak of (0.004 mm). A millimetre either side wraps the same words into one long line and one short, or three with a widow, so re-measure if the words or BodyFontMm change. Lantern Designer's terms cell is 57. Never drawn narrower than the code and its margins, and never wider than a third of the strip, which is the logo cell's own cap.",
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellTextGapMm": 1,
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellTextGapMmNote": "The note stops this far short of the code's quiet zone. The zone alone is 0.61 mm, and a line of type ending that close to the symbol reads as touching it.",
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellNoteMinFieldRoomMm": 250,
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellNoteMinFieldRoomMmNote": "ON NARROW PAPER THE NOTE GOES BEFORE ANY FIELD IS CUT. If the whole cell would leave the fields less strip than this, the cell is drawn COMPACT instead: the code at its full size with Note CompactText turned up its left side, 12.4 mm wide in place of 56. Measured in Open Sans on 19-Sep-2026, a sheet's fields need from 193 mm at their text (PS01 with a short title) to 299 mm (a long client, three scales and an 84 character title). So 250 keeps the note on A3 landscape and everything larger - the fields are left 314 mm, which holds the worst of those whole - and drops it on A4 landscape and A3 portrait, where the whole cell would leave 191 mm and the compact one leaves 235; and on A4 portrait. The test is the paper's width and nothing on the sheet, on purpose: every sheet of one size in a pack is then drawn the same way, whatever its title runs to. 0 never goes compact.",
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellCompactFontMm": 1.6,
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellCompactMinFontMm": 1.2,
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellCompactPaddingMm": 1.2,
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellCompactNote": "The compact caption is bold, takes the labels' uppercasing and tracking, and reads upward, its baseline on the edge of the code's quiet zone and its capitals standing clear of it to the left. CompactPaddingMm is the clear paper between those capitals and the cell's rule. It has only the code's own 8.79 mm to run along: a caption that will not fit at CompactFontMm is set smaller rather than cut, because half an instruction is no instruction, and one that would have to go under CompactMinFontMm is left out altogether with the band it would have stood in - a code with no caption is still a code, and print too small to read is not a caption. The shipped '3D MODEL' fits at the full 1.6.",
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellPaddingHMm": 1.4,
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellPaddingVMm": 1.1,
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellPaddingNote": "PaddingHMm is the fields' own FieldPaddingHMm, so the note starts where a field's label would. PaddingVMm is Lantern Designer's: the most the note's block may fill of the strip's height before it loses a line.",
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellHeadingFontMm": 2,
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellBodyFontMm": 1.5,
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellFontNote": "Lantern Designer's heading size, bold, with the labels' uppercasing and tracking, so the cell reads as part of the title block rather than as a sticker on it. The body is regular and muted, and 1.5 where Lantern's is 1.3: it is a lowercase sentence that a client has to be able to read, and two lines of it leave the strip room to spare. It inverts the caption-over-value rhythm of the field cells on purpose - those caption a value the reader is looking for, this one tells them to do something, so the instruction leads.",
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellLineSpacing": 1.22,
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellHeadingGapMm": 0.3,
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellBodyMaxLines": 4,
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellBodyMaxLinesNote": "The most body lines ever set; fewer when the strip is too low for them (at 10 mm, three fit under the heading). Copy that will not fit ends in an ellipsis rather than overflowing the strip, which on a title block would read as a printing fault. The heading and body are centred in the strip's height as one block, measured from the top of the heading's capitals to the last baseline, so it sits level with the code beside it.",
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellBodyJustify": true,
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellJustifyMaxTrackingMm": 0.1,
+        "LayoutEditor__TitleBlock__QrCellJustifyNote": "Every body line but the last is stretched to the column by letter spacing, so the note reads as a block with a flush right edge beside a square code (Lantern Designer's terms cell does the same). ALL OF THEM OR NONE: if any line would need more than JustifyMaxTrackingMm after every character, the whole block is left at its natural spacing - one flush line over one ragged one reads as a fault, where a wholly ragged block reads as a choice.",
