-    "LayoutEditor__Dimensions__Config"    : {
-        "LayoutEditor__Dimensions__Description"          : "Sheet dimensions (D32) drawn in paper millimetres. A dimension placed over a 2D viewport reports paper length times the viewport's scale denominator, so it measures the model; elsewhere it reports paper millimetres. Precision is decimal places; the units suffix follows the figure. ORTHO: hold Shift while the line is being placed (after the second click) and the dimension runs horizontal or vertical whatever its two points are - drag the line above or below them for the x distance between them, beside them for the y. Release Shift and it is aligned again. The record keeps this as Dimension__Orientation ('aligned', 'horizontal' or 'vertical'; a record from before it is aligned). The offset is measured from the start point, and an ortho line stays where it was put while a grip re-picks either point. SIZE MM (TickLengthMm, MinTickLengthMm, MaxTickLengthMm): how large the ticks, arrows or dots at each end are, in paper millimetres. The Dimensions panel's Size mm row, under Ends, sets it per dimension; the record keeps it as Dimension__TickLengthMm. A record from before it has no key and draws at TickLengthMm.",
