-    "LayoutEditor__WebViewer__Config"     : {
-        "LayoutEditor__WebViewer__Description"           : "The read-only document viewer the live web build shows in place of the editor. Where authoring is off - anywhere but localhost or an explicitly unlocked device - the panel columns, toolbar and measurements box are never built, and the drawings and the project specification are read as one cycled list of documents with a dock at the bottom of the screen. The tab strip is unchanged: it is the same strip the editor has, scrolling sideways with an arrow at each end once the tabs do not all fit. Enabled false hands the web build back the read-only editor it had before this existed. ShowSpecification false leaves the specification out of the cycle. SwipeMinPx is how far a finger has to travel PAST the edge of the paper before the document changes, so panning a zoomed drawing never turns the page by accident. DoubleTapZoomFactor is how much closer a double tap on a fitted sheet brings it; a double tap on an already magnified sheet fits it again.",
