-    "LayoutEditor__Snapping__Config"      : {
-        "LayoutEditor__Snapping__Description"  : "Object snaps for placing and dragging dimensions and drawing vectors. Two sources: the projected linework inside 2D viewports, and - with SheetObjects on - the sheet's own vectors and dimensions, so a new line can start on the corner of the last one and a polygon can close exactly on its first point. A dragged vector snaps too: the grab point and every vertex are offered, and the nearest snap moves the whole shape. RadiusPx is the pick radius on screen at any zoom. Endpoints and midpoints are candidates; an endpoint wins a near tie, and the sheet's own markup wins a tie with the linework because it sits on top. The item being dragged never offers its own moving point. HiddenLines adds the hidden class as a source. The toggle (toolbar button or the Snap__Toggle key binding) is remembered per browser. MARKER COLOURS say which tool is snapping: blue for vertices (the Draw and Rectangle tools, vertex grips, and a vector being moved), orange for dimensions (the Dimension tool, its grips and its line inference); purple is the viewport tone, for carrying a viewport by a point once TrueVision's viewport snap move is ported. The colours live in Na__LayoutEditor__Styles__Main__.css.",
-        "LayoutEditor__Snapping__Enabled"      : true,
-        "LayoutEditor__Snapping__RadiusPx"     : 14,
-        "LayoutEditor__Snapping__Endpoints"    : true,
-        "LayoutEditor__Snapping__Midpoints"    : true,
-        "LayoutEditor__Snapping__HiddenLines"  : false,
-        "LayoutEditor__Snapping__SheetObjects" : true,
-        "LayoutEditor__Snapping__MarkerSizePx" : 18
