-    "LayoutEditor__Clipboard__Config"     : {
-        "LayoutEditor__Clipboard__Description"   : "Copy, paste and duplicate for viewports, vectors, text, groups, and a multi-selection of vectors or text (Ctrl+C, Ctrl+V, Ctrl+D, and the right-click menu). A paste is a new item with a fresh id: a viewport also gets a new name ('{name} copy', then '{name} copy 2' - wording in the Labels block) and every other setting of the one copied; a vector keeps its vertices, closed, edges, fill, gradient and opacities, offset by PasteOffsetMm. Text, groups and a multi-selection paste the same way, with group members remapped to the new ids. A viewport arrives unlocked. On the sheet it was copied from it steps PasteOffsetMm down and right of the original, and again past any copy already there; on another sheet it lands in the same place; from the menu on bare paper its top-left corner goes at the click. Pointing a viewport copy at a different scene clears the copy name so the caption follows the new scene. CopySnapshot lets a 3D copy show the original's stored picture straight away instead of rendering it again. One paste is one undo step. The clipboard is this tab's memory: it survives changing sheet, not a reload.",
