+    "LayoutEditor__Navigation__Config": {
+        "LayoutEditor__Navigation__Description": "Wheel zooms about the cursor; middle or right drag pans; touch pinches. Left click is for editing.",
+        "LayoutEditor__Navigation__ZoomMin": 0.15,
+        "LayoutEditor__Navigation__ZoomMax": 8,
+        "LayoutEditor__Navigation__AuthoringZoomMaxNote": "HOW CLOSE, AND FOR WHOM - Adam, 21-Sep-2026: 'I can't get close enough into things... make an exception for the local host version'. The viewers do not need to zoom that far, and the live web should not have to keep drawing huge zooms. ZoomMax is a reader's ceiling: the web document viewer's, and any session's that may not author. AuthoringZoomMax is the ceiling wherever authoring is on - localhost, or a device unlocked with ?authoring=on - and is never taken below ZoomMax. Zoom 1 puts ScreenPixelsPerMm (3.2) screen pixels on a paper millimetre, so 8 is 25.6 px to the millimetre and 64 is 205: a 20 mm frame member drawn at 1:100 is 5 px across at 8 and 41 px at 64. Lines keep their printed weight as the sheet grows, as they do in LayOut; Draft mode (K) draws them one pixel wide at any zoom.",
+        "LayoutEditor__Navigation__AuthoringZoomMax": 64,
+        "LayoutEditor__Navigation__ZoomWheelStep": 0.0016,
+        "LayoutEditor__Navigation__FitPaddingPx": 32,
+        "LayoutEditor__Navigation__ZoomSettleNote": "ZOOM NOW, REDRAW WHEN IT RESTS - Adam, 21-Sep-2026: 'there should be a debounce, so it waits a little bit after you stop zooming before it tries to redraw'. A wheel or pinch zoom only changes the paper's scale while it is under way; ZoomSettleMs after the last step the zoom 'settles' once, and everything that follows the zoom happens then, together: the selection handles and grips are counter-scaled again, the notes margin grip, group boxes, eyedropper boxes and the Measurements box are placed, Draft mode's hairlines are re-solved - and the sheet is drawn again, crisp, at its new zoom. Wheel steps are also gathered into one per animation frame. A single zoom (Fit, 100%, a resize) settles at once. 100 to 3000; LayOut's own Pan and Zoom Redraw Delay defaults to 300.",
+        "LayoutEditor__Navigation__ZoomSettleMs": 350,
+        "LayoutEditor__Navigation__HoldPaperWhileZoomingNote": "While a zoom gesture is under way the paper is held as one composited layer (will-change: transform), so each step scales the picture already drawn instead of rasterising every line, fill, hatch and picture on the sheet again; it is drawn crisp once, when the zoom settles. Measured on RB05's ground floor plan in headless Chrome: 76-110 ms a zoom step without it, 17-20 ms (50-60 frames a second) with it, zooming in and out alike. The sheet is soft while the wheel turns and sharp a moment after. False rasterises every step, as before.",
+        "LayoutEditor__Navigation__HoldPaperWhileZooming": true
+    },
+
+    "LayoutEditor__WebViewer__Config": {
+        "LayoutEditor__WebViewer__Description": "The read-only document viewer the live web build shows in place of the editor. Where authoring is off - anywhere but localhost or an explicitly unlocked device - the drawing tabs, panel columns, toolbar and measurements box are never built, and the drawings and the project specification are shown as one cycled list of documents with a bar at the top and a dock at the bottom. Enabled false hands the web build back the read-only editor it had before this existed. ShowSpecification false leaves the specification out of the list entirely. SwipeMinPx is how far a finger has to travel PAST the edge of the paper before the document changes, so panning a zoomed drawing never turns the page by accident. DoubleTapZoomFactor is how much closer a double tap on a fitted sheet brings it; a double tap on an already magnified sheet fits it again.",
