+        "LayoutEditor__Shapes__Description": "The Draw tool's vector shapes (lines, polylines, polygons) and the Rectangle tool's rectangles, which are ordinary closed four-point shapes once drawn. Defaults for a new shape; the Vectors panel edits them. CloseRadiusPx is how near the first point a click has to land to close a polygon. DefaultStroked draws the edges; with it off a new shape is its fill alone, so DefaultFilled must be on as well or the shape would have nothing to show. Dashed edges are off by default; the toggle and its millimetre figures live in Na__LayoutEditor__LineStyleTool__Config__.json.",
+        "LayoutEditor__Shapes__DefaultStrokeColour": "#172b3a",
+        "LayoutEditor__Shapes__DefaultStrokePt": 0.20,
+        "LayoutEditor__Shapes__DefaultStroked": true,
+        "LayoutEditor__Shapes__DefaultFillColour": "#e4e8ec",
+        "LayoutEditor__Shapes__DefaultFilled": false,
+        "LayoutEditor__Shapes__DefaultFillOpacity": 1,
+        "LayoutEditor__Shapes__TransparentEdgeOpacity": 0.5,
+        "LayoutEditor__Shapes__OpacityNote": "Opacity runs from 0 (clear) to 1 (solid). DefaultFillOpacity is how solid a new shape's fill is - the Vectors panel's Fill opacity slider. Edges are solid unless Transparent edges is ticked; TransparentEdgeOpacity is where the Edge opacity slider starts when it is. A gradient keeps its own alpha. Shapes from before opacity existed are solid.",
+        "LayoutEditor__Shapes__LineStyleNote": "Dashed edges - a toggle on the Vectors panel, off by default. On, the Draw and Rectangle tools place dashed, dotted or dash-dot (centre) lines, with the section lengths in paper millimetres and a scale that stretches them. Owned by Na__LayoutEditor__LineStyleTool__. A shape from before the toggle is a solid line.",
