+        "LayoutEditor__Leader__ShapeNote": "The curve and the heads. StubMm is the straight run level with each end, capped at StubMaxFraction of the leader's horizontal run so a short leader is not all stub. CurveTension is how far along the run the S-curve's control points reach: 0.5 is an even S, lower is tighter at the ends. TextGapMm is the clear paper between the line's end and a note's text, TextPaddingMm pads a note's fill, and LineSpacing is a note's line height as a multiple of its text size. TextAttach 'first-line' lands the line level with the middle of a note's first line (the CAD default); 'middle' lands it on the middle of the whole note. BubblePaddingMm is the clearance a code keeps inside its bubble before the bubble grows to fit it. MinLengthMm is how far from the point the head has to be before a leader exists.",
