-    "LayoutEditor__Measurements__Config"  : {
-        "LayoutEditor__Measurements__Description"   : "The Measurements box at the bottom right of the sheet (Na__LayoutEditor__Measurements__), SketchUp's VCB. While the Draw, Rectangle or Dimension tool is up it reads out what is being drawn as it is drawn - a line's length, a rectangle's width x height, a dimension's span and then its line's offset - and a value typed while drawing is used on Enter, with no click into the box first: Draw places the next point that far along the rubber band (its direction, so snaps, Shift and the arrow key axis lock aim it); Rectangle lands the opposite corner (3000 x 2000 or 3000,2000; one figure is a square; typed straight after a rectangle lands, it resizes that rectangle); Dimension picks the end that far along the band, then puts the line that far from what it measures. Dragging a vertex of a finished vector wakes the box the same way: the reading is the drag's length, and a typed value moves the vertex that far along the inferred direction (the original vertex toward where it is being dragged; a minus sign runs the other way) and finishes the drag so the pointer cannot pull it back. Dragging a viewport's frame (not a handle, not the drawing inside) wakes it too: a typed value moves the frame that far along the drag, at the viewport's scale (or the sheet's for a 3D viewport). A number with no unit is millimetres; add m, cm or mm for another (2.5m), commas may group thousands (2,500) and a minus sign draws the other way. The line above the box shows how a value is being read as it is typed. AT SCALE: with atScale true on the shape and dimension defaults, lines, rectangles and a dragged vertex take and show real sizes at the drawing's scale - the 2D viewport under the first point (or the vertex), or the sheet's scale elsewhere - so 2500 at 1:50 is 50 mm of paper. A dimension uses the same. The chip at the right of the box shows the scale in use. Precision is the decimal places a reading shows (trailing zeros dropped), UnitsSuffix follows it, PairSeparator joins a rectangle's two sizes, HintMs is how long a message above the box stays, and EdgeGapPx keeps the box clear of the stage's scrollbars. The keys it reads are in Na__Hotkeys__DrawingTabs__.json under MeasurementsBox. The Vectors/Dimensions panel toggle rows are not here: atScale is hardcoded true so DrawingScale works.",
-        "LayoutEditor__Measurements__Enabled"       : true,
-        "LayoutEditor__Measurements__Precision"     : 1,
-        "LayoutEditor__Measurements__UnitsSuffix"   : " mm",
-        "LayoutEditor__Measurements__PairSeparator" : " x ",
-        "LayoutEditor__Measurements__HintMs"        : 2800,
-        "LayoutEditor__Measurements__EdgeGapPx"     : 10
-    },
