+    "LayoutEditor__Specification__Config": {
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__Description": "The Project Specification tab: every drawing note of the project, in groups. A group has a prefix (GN, SN, EE) and a title; a note has a title and its specification text. A note's code is its group's prefix and its place in the group, zero-padded to NumberDigits - GN01, EE02 - so moving a note up or down, moving it to another group or changing its group's prefix renumbers it. Specification bubbles on the sheets link to a note by its id, not its code, so a renumber reaches every bubble on every sheet. The specification is a file of its own (FileName) beside project.json, kept locally in the project folder so an agent can edit it on disk, and written to the same R2 key on Sync. LegacyFileName is the previous R2 name, read only when FileName is not there yet. The file is read when the drawing editor opens. Every edit is kept in this browser at once (DraftEnabled, written DraftDebounceMs after the typing pauses); Sync writes the whole file to R2 and to the local copy, and first asks whether to replace a cloud copy that changed since it was read (ConfirmCloudOverwrite). HistorySteps is the tab's own undo depth.",
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__FileName": "ValeVision__DrawingNotes__.json",
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__LegacyFileName": "",
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__NumberDigits": 2,
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__RevisionNote": "The specification is a document that gets issued, so it carries a revision and a number of its own, the way each sheet carries a Rev and a Drawing No. Both are typed in the Project Specification bar, both print on the document, and both name the downloaded file through the shared Pdf FilenamePattern. DefaultRevision is what an untouched specification opens at, and what a specification written before these fields existed is read as. DocumentNumberSuffix is appended to the project code when no number has been typed, so PS01 gives PS01_SPEC.",
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__DefaultRevision": "A",
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__RevisionMaxLength": 6,
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__DocumentNumberSuffix": "_SPEC",
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__DocumentName": "Project Specification",
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__DownloadPaperSize": "A4",
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__PrefixMaxLength": 4,
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__DraftEnabled": true,
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__DraftDebounceMs": 600,
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__HistorySteps": 50,
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__LoadTimeoutMs": 12000,
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__ConfirmCloudOverwrite": true,
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__LockstepEnabled": true,
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__LockstepPollMs": 3000,
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__AutoSaveLocalMs": 4000,
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__LockstepNote": "Keeps the specification in the app and its local file (FileName) in step, as the Statement Writer does with a statement's markdown. Agents and hand edits change the local file directly, so on localhost the app looks at it on load, every LockstepPollMs while the drawing editor is open, when the window gets the focus back, and immediately before every write - the autosave, Enter in the drawing's Specification tab, Save Sheets and Sync. If the file no longer holds what the app last read or wrote, nothing is written and the app asks which copy to keep - its own (kept in this browser as a JSON draft) or the file - showing when each last changed and which notes differ. The copy not chosen is kept in this browser (Na__LayoutEditor__SpecDiscarded__<code>). What is in the app is written to the file AutoSaveLocalMs after the editing pauses (0 turns that off), so an agent always starts from what is on screen; R2 is still written only by Save Sheets and Sync. Whether the copies agree is decided by their content, not by each note's stamp; the times only explain. Set LockstepEnabled false to go back to the last save winning (the autosave to the file stops with it).",
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__StarterGroupsNote": "The groups Add standard groups creates on a project with no specification. IsGeneral marks a group of general notes: they are listed on every sheet's notes margin, after the notes that sheet's bubbles link to.",
+        "LayoutEditor__Specification__StarterGroups": [
+            { "Prefix": "GN", "Title": "General Notes", "IsGeneral": true },
+            { "Prefix": "SN", "Title": "Structural Notes", "IsGeneral": false },
+            { "Prefix": "FN", "Title": "Finishes", "IsGeneral": false }
