+    "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__Config": {
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__Description": "The notes margin a sheet can carry down its right-hand side, from the top of the border to the title block. Switched on per sheet with the Notes button on the toolbar or in the Margin Notes panel; drag its left edge to make it wider or narrower. It lists the specification notes the sheet's bubbles link to, in specification order, then the general notes. Distances and text sizes are paper millimetres except the divider and rule (printed points). TextSizeMm is the body (2 mm); titles are TitleScale times that. PaddingMm is the left and top/foot inset; PaddingRightMm is the clearance before the sheet's right border, a little more so wrapped lines do not clip. A note reads as its code, CodePipe, then its title, with the body wrapped to the full inner width. A faint RuleColour line at RulePt sits between notes, centred in the gap between them: NoteGapMm is the least that gap can be, and decides what fits; when every note fits and the column has room left at the foot, every gap opens by the same amount, up to NoteGapMaxMm. IncludeGeneralNotes and GroupHeadings are what a newly switched-on margin starts with.",
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__DefaultWidthMm": 90,
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__MinWidthMm": 40,
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__MaxWidthFraction": 0.6,
