+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__CodeGapMm": 2,
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__CodePipe": " | ",
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__GroupGapMm": 2,
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__DividerPt": 0.5,
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__RulePt": 0.35,
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__RuleColour": "#cfd4d8",
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__IncludeGeneralNotes": true,
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__GroupHeadings": false,
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__GripWidthPx": 10,
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__RegionsNote": "Overspill Note Regions: boxes drawn on the sheet that hold notes too, switched on per sheet with Overspill Note Regions in the Margin Notes panel and each drawn by dragging a box, snapping as the Rectangle tool does. A region lists the notes of the groups ticked in it, which then leave the margin (a group ticked in two goes to the first), and a region with Overspill ticked takes whatever did not fit where it was meant to go, in specification order - the margin's tail first of all - after its own groups. With the margin off, every note no region claims waits for the overspill regions. A region is painted paper like the margin, laid out by the margin's rules at the margin's text size, with RegionPaddingMm inside it on every side; it is never smaller than RegionMinSizeMm either way. Its border lines are the margin's divider (DividerPt, in the ink colour), each side switched on its own; RegionBordersDefault is whether a new region starts with all four. Its title is the one typed, else RegionOverspillTitle for an overspill region, a lone group's own title, or RegionGroupsTitle. RegionGripPx is the on-screen reach of its edge and corner grips.",
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__RegionMinSizeMm": 15,
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__RegionPaddingMm": 3,
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__RegionOverspillTitle": "NOTES (CONTINUED)",
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__RegionGroupsTitle": "NOTES",
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__RegionBordersDefault": true,
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__RegionGripPx": 10,
+        "LayoutEditor__MarginNotes__LeaderlessNote": "Leaderless Notes: whole specification groups a sheet lists whether or not a bubble on it links to them - a project introduction, or a block of notes that needs no leader. Switched on per sheet with Leaderless Notes in the Margin Notes panel, where each group is ticked; the ticked groups form a stack whose order is the print order, dragged by a grip (or moved with the arrow keys on it), and a group ticked joins the foot of the stack. They are listed FIRST, before the notes the sheet's bubbles link to and the general notes, each group's notes in specification order; a note of theirs a bubble links to as well is listed once, in its group's place. Everything else is as for any note: the margin's text size and group headings, a region ticking the group takes its notes, and what does not fit carries on in the overspill regions. Switching it off keeps the ticked groups and their order. The sheet keeps them on its notes margin record as LeaderlessOn and LeaderlessGroups."
+    },
